{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e810950cea6e1bdef6960fab4d3899639598231cbb318032343fdc246c37287c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet us define the pushforward of a presheaf.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e4ed53aaef07d50b58015d083e190766298c2ee35927f8ca9c3941e18e0d6274", "unit_id": "tag:03PV:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f: X\\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} $", "MATH_0003": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_*\\mathcal{F} : Y_\\etale^{opp} \\longrightarrow \\textit{Sets}, \\quad\n(V/Y) \\longmapsto \\mathcal{F}(X \\times_Y V/X).\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$f_* = f_{small, *}$", "MATH_0008": "$f_{big, *}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-direct-image-presheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:904ef9f8656ee74cab8edd3f48c28025e8d1f868d20fce4190a09bf226b37497", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f85f9f342040ea438b0aa549178d074897dea083e88bad88a8bbe5b78d16b57", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> a presheaf of sets on <MATH_0003>.\nThe <TEXTITOPEN_0001>direct image<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>, or <TEXTITOPEN_0002>pushforward<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> of <MATH_0004>\n(under <MATH_0005>) is\n<MATH_0006>\nWe sometimes write <MATH_0007> to distinguish from other\ndirect image functors (such as usual Zariski pushforward or <MATH_0008>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:355baabde257d5247597f60e3b223b6f6fec0fb1297857107da70af19e88c55f", "unit_id": "tag:03PW:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\circ u$", "MATH_0003": "$u$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\nf_* = f_{small, *} :\n\\textit{PSh}(X_\\etale)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{PSh}(Y_\\etale)\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\nf_* = f_{small, *} :\n\\textit{PAb}(X_\\etale)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\textit{PAb}(Y_\\etale)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-functorial}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b89b7a18fc3efeb4beb82b15bb49ddba5684519a3b680397853ea0d1deb6df96", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c5be0ea2a179a4456f8446cd979e756b379ce6e6c5fb6dceafa06b9ba5d4da5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is a well-defined <ACCENT_0001>tale presheaf since the base change of an <ACCENT_0002>tale\nmorphism is again <ACCENT_0003>tale. A more categorical way of saying this is that\n<MATH_0001> is the composition of functors <MATH_0002>\nwhere <MATH_0003> is as in Equation (<REF_0001>). This makes it\nclear that the construction is functorial in the presheaf\n<MATH_0004> and hence we obtain a functor\n<MATH_0005>\nNote that if <MATH_0006> is a presheaf of abelian groups, then\n<MATH_0007> is also a presheaf of abelian groups and we obtain\n<MATH_0008>\nas before (i.e., defined by exactly the same rule).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1facec6d6b3e55869d1bedb7aad34724c0c5623176f50f7ae6447118383a3637", "unit_id": "tag:03PV:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03PV", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\{V_j \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$Y_\\etale$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{X \\times_Y V_j \\to X \\times_Y V\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$X_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{X \\times_Y V_i \\to X \\times_Y V\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-direct-image-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:10132884520cb962dca2e1464b36326c52e22815a2883c8575f0e2c74b7c1362", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c615cdf36b0cd66f2e0348c772778fbbaa8e35db583ea7c9ee4c416011ae44de", "source_text": "We claim that the direct image of a sheaf is a sheaf.\nNamely, if <MATH_0001> is an <ACCENT_0001>tale covering in <MATH_0002>\nthen <MATH_0003> is an <ACCENT_0002>tale covering in\n<MATH_0004>. Hence the sheaf condition for <MATH_0005> with respect\nto <MATH_0006>\nis equivalent to the sheaf condition for <MATH_0007> with respect to\n<MATH_0008>. Thus if <MATH_0009> is a sheaf, so is\n<MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:60f95b44e0fda07af3e9d608c289c22b200a289ae1e78e534af011b2083bbda1", "unit_id": "tag:03PX:statement"}
